@startuml
title OSLF composition: the logic axis and the resource axis converge on one COMM verdict

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
  DiamondBorderColor #1F2937
  DiamondFontColor #111827
}

|#DCFCE7|Logic axis|
start
:guard φ\n(predicate algebra); <<#BBF7D0>>
:guard-satisfied?\n(structural ∧ behavioral); <<#BBF7D0>>

|#E0E7FF|Resource axis|
:demand Δ, supply Σ, margin\n(OSLF); <<#E0E7FF>>
:is_funded = Δ + margin ≤ Σ?; <<#E0E7FF>>

|#FCE7F3|COMM verdict|
:COMM fires ⟺\nguard-satisfied ∧ funded; <<#FBCFE8>>
stop

note right
  Two DISTINCT effective theories that COMPOSE at the
  guarded-COMM boundary — not one fused theorem, but a
  conjunction of two independently-proven verdicts at one
  point. Both proven in the same zero-admission rho_bridge
  tree (RhoGuardedCommSoundness.v · MettaOslfLawsConformance.v).
  reject-underfunded ≈ reject-safe: neither grants on absence
  of evidence.
end note

legend right
|= Lane / color |= Axis |
|<#DCFCE7> Logic axis | the predicate algebra — is the COMM enabled? |
|<#E0E7FF> Resource axis | OSLF funding — is the rewrite affordable? |
|<#FCE7F3> COMM verdict | both axes converge: guard-satisfied ∧ funded |
endlegend
@enduml
